 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Use **`@needs_app_scope`**, defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps the callback so it runs inside the app context. Decorate a plain `@click.command(...)` with it, as `shell_command` and `routes_command` do (`src/tessel/cli.py:998-1000`, `1047-1059`).\n\nIf you register the command on the app's CLI group (`@app.cli.command(...)`), the wrapping is automatic through `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413-427`), so you don't need the decorator.\n\nThe class that loads the app is **`LaunchInfo`** (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`), via its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`). It finds the app from the `create_app` callable, the import path, or `wsgi.py`/`app.py`. If you need the object directly rather than the context, use `@pass_script_info` (`src/tessel/cli.py:375`), as `run_command` does (`src/tessel/cli.py:933`).",
